## Task: Motor Start/Stop with Seal-In Control

The conveyor is driven by motor **M1**. Use the two pushbuttons on the control panel to control the motor:

1. Press **Start** (green, NO contact) to start the motor. After you release the button, the motor must **keep running** (seal-in);
2. Press **Stop** (red) to stop the motor. Note that the Stop button is **normally closed**: when it is not pressed, `STOP` = 1; when pressed, it = 0. So in the ladder diagram, draw STOP as an **NO contact -| |-** (in ST, write `AND STOP`). If you draw it as an NC contact -|/|-, it will be open even when not pressed, so the motor will not run when you press Start;
3. If Start and Stop are pressed at the same time, **Stop takes priority**;
4. If the motor overloads, the thermal overload relay trips (`M1_OL_OK` changes to 0), and the motor must stop immediately. After the thermal overload relay is reset, the motor **must not restart automatically**; Start must be pressed again;
5. The **Run indicator lamp** is on while the motor is running.

